# Roblox Luau Style

## Strings

- Prefer Roblox backtick interpolation.
- Do not introduce `string.format` when interpolation is enough.

```lua
local text = `{player.Name} dealt {damage} damage`
```

## Code shape

- Prefer direct, readable modules over unnecessary abstraction.
- Keep lifecycle and entry methods easy to find near the top when the repository uses them.
- Keep helper functions near the end of the file instead of scattering them above the main flow.
- Group helpers only when that improves scanability.
- Do not predeclare local function variables unless there is a real need; direct Luau function definitions are preferred.
- Push pure logic into helper modules instead of growing entry files indefinitely.
- Follow the repository's existing file layout instead of forcing a new one.
- Only extract a helper when logic is reused, non-trivial, or noticeably clearer after extraction.
- Do not wrap simple one-off logic in tiny helper functions when inline code is easier to read.
- Prefer explicit, readable control flow over compact or clever patterns.

## Deterministic paths and config

- Do not add defensive nil guards around resource paths, config paths, or owned assets when the path is deterministic by project design.
- Use defensive checks only for truly optional state, runtime timing issues, or user-driven absence.

## Consistency

- Match the naming and structure already used by the surrounding system.
- Reuse existing helpers and project conventions before adding new patterns.
